Install and update MariaDB's dev plugin

On its first start the extension installs MariaDB's dev plugin
(github.com/mariadb/ai-plugins, folder dev) with the bundled CLI:
`extensions install https://github.com/mariadb/ai-plugins:dev --consent
--auto-update`. A plugin already in <QWEN_HOME or ~/.qwen>/extensions/dev
counts as installed; if it came from that repository without an autoUpdate
field, it gets autoUpdate: true once. Done is recorded in globalState
(mariadbDevPluginInstalled), so an uninstalled plugin stays uninstalled; a
failed install (offline) is only logged and retried on the next start.

On every start the extension then runs `extensions update <name> --consent`
for each user extension whose install metadata has autoUpdate: true (as the
terminal UI does at startup). `extensions update` gets --consent for that,
like `extensions install`. Failures are logged and retried on the next start.

All of it runs in the background; the daemon and the ACP process wait for it
before they start, so they load the installed or updated plugin. The setting
qwen-code.installMariaDbPlugin (on by default) turns off install and updates.

